    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d635">

                <pb facs="0547" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg431"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.124/220.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Chargé d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase,]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Say to the Minister for Foreign Affairs that there are objections to the proposed
                    convention, set forth in your July 28; and that before entering into any
                    convention it is highly desirable to make the preliminary investigation, the
                    result of which would probably compensate Ecuador fully for the outlay.
                    Ascertain whether in the absence of negotiation of a convention the $8100 will
                    be available.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
